--- !u!114 &1796869838
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1796869833}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 131c3d2a5c4bbb64d99389ceda1fd2a5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MetaMove.Demo.Kitting.StoryDirector
  cell: {fileID: 1796869840}
  speed: {fileID: 867426346}
  card: {fileID: 1294967311}
  voiceSource: {fileID: 1796869836}
  beats:
  - key: welcome
    title: The line is running
    caption: We couldn't bring you to the factory, so we brought the factory to you.
      Welcome to MetaMove. This is an ABB GoFa, a collaborative robot, life-size.
      Right now, it is packing gear kits. Watch it work for a moment.
    image: {fileID: 0}
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: dffd3dd0db8a4794c81b6fa6f9372693, type: 3}
    hold: 0
  - key: story
    title: No fence
    caption: 'Cobots are usually kept slow everywhere, just in case someone comes
      close. Safe, but it wastes most of the robot. MetaMove adds a distance-based
      speed-scaling safety layer: it knows where you are, so the arm runs at full
      speed until you come near.'
    image: {fileID: 0}
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d8f934f35348df245ab908883279a275, type: 3}
    hold: 14
  - key: tracking
    title: How it knows
    caption: How does it know? The QR code on the post is the spatial anchor. The
      headset's own SLAM tracking finds it, and the code is measured to the robot
      base. So your head and hands are known relative to the robot, and that distance
      sets the speed.
    image: {fileID: 0}
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: fecda5cf808ca424590b7a646808b8bd, type: 3}
    hold: 16
  - key: refill
    title: Bring the next batch
    caption: The tray is getting low. The next batch is waiting on the trolley on
      your left, in the orange box. Pick it up and load it into the rack, while the
      arm keeps working.
    image: {fileID: 0}
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4c7dc3d538b7e20448590ee4ae13829d, type: 3}
    hold: 0
  - key: slow
    title: It knows you are there
    caption: Notice the arm slowing down as you come closer? That is distance-based
      speed scaling. The closer you are, the slower it moves. Nothing personal.
    image: {fileID: 0}
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 51861189ba7987346952106a783d9bfc, type: 3}
    hold: 9
  - key: standstill
    title: Standstill
    caption: And now it stops. Nothing broke. You are inside its reach, and it would
      rather wait than meet you.
    image: {fileID: 0}
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: deef2366e1320d243a3cec2c91570c5e, type: 3}
    hold: 6
  - key: stepback
    title: A step back, please
    caption: Would you be so kind as to take a step back? Then the arm can carry
      on, and I can finish showing you around.
    image: {fileID: 0}
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: fd31e2011b2cb684abec5530686877e3, type: 3}
    hold: 7
  - key: recover
    title: Trust comes back slowly
    caption: Step back. Notice it does not rush off straight away?
    image: {fileID: 0}
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b5fccda16dc69d4459345d01b4fe8af3, type: 3}
    hold: 9
  - key: empty
    title: Clear the empty box
    caption: The first box is empty. The arm noticed and switched to the reserve
      box on the left, so the line keeps running. Take the empty box out at the front
      and put it on the return lane below. Watch the arm while your hands are close.
    image: {fileID: 0}
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 409f8804038945a4ca237fce4e21140d, type: 3}
    hold: 0
  - key: guide
    title: Show it the new tray
    caption: 'The new box sits in a lane the arm has never seen. Instead of programming
      it, show it. Reach out with an open hand to the cyan sphere on the tool. Pinch
      it between thumb and index finger, and keep pinching while you move your hand:
      the arm follows. Bring it over the orange box, roughly is enough. Then raise
      your left hand, palm up, and press Teach in the hand menu.'
    image: {fileID: 0}
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 464d848eb65fe41458a091471a9563ae, type: 3}
    hold: 0
  - key: grab
    title: Hand guiding
    caption: Steady. I will follow your hand anywhere, except into the rack. Someone
      has to be sensible here.
    image: {fileID: 0}
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d7f063d3deb626746b6dabe706b43355, type: 3}
    hold: 7
  - key: aligned
    title: Taught
    caption: Found it, and lined up to the millimetre. You gave the intent, the machine
      added the precision.
    image: {fileID: 0}
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 0855d0ae18e33944295204a17b61ba55, type: 3}
    hold: 6
  - key: release
    title: Hand it back
    caption: 'The line runs again from the box you just showed it, at full speed
      now that you are clear. That is MetaMove: careful when you are close, fast
      when you are not, and taught without a single line of code.'
    image: {fileID: 0}
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9d8644425b9b5d04784399e53a7572a6, type: 3}
    hold: 12
  gapAfterLine: 3
  lingerAfterLine: 3
--- !u!114 &1796869839
MonoBehaviour:
